COMPONENT - Computah OS library
(generated from docs/API.md)

The OS adds *primary components* to the machine's
component library: for each type, one component is
the default (the first found, or the one chosen
with setPrimary). All the raw functions (list,
invoke, proxy, type, slot, methods, doc, get,
fields) are unchanged; see LUA.md.

component.isAvailable(type) -> boolean

Whether a component of this type is available
(that is, there is a primary one).

- type (string): a component type such as "gpu" or
  "modem".

  if component.isAvailable("modem") then print("networking available") end

component.getPrimary(type[, quiet]) -> proxy

The proxy of the primary component of a type. The
first call picks the first component of that type
found; when it is removed, the next call picks
another.

- type (string): component type.
- quiet (boolean): return nil instead of raising
  an error when there is none.
- Errors: no primary '<type>' available (unless
  quiet).

  local gpu = component.getPrimary("gpu")
  gpu.set(1, 1, "hello")

component.setPrimary(type, address)

Makes a component the primary one of its type, or
with address = nil forgets the choice (the next
getPrimary picks the first one found again).
Pushes a component_available signal.

- address (string or nil): full address or a
  unique prefix.

component.isPrimary(address) -> boolean

Whether the component with this address is the
primary one of its type.

Primary components as fields

component.<type> is shorthand for
component.getPrimary("<type>", true):
component.gpu, component.modem, component.eeprom,
component.redstone, ... It is nil when there is no
component of that type.

  component.gpu.setForeground(0xFF0000)

Signals

Signal - Values - When
component_available - type - a component of a type
    without a primary appears, or setPrimary was
    called
component_unavailable - type - the primary
    component of a type is removed
